    "description": "I need to pull my own images out of a photography app that blocks screenshots and offers no in-app export. The app is installed on both an iPhone and an Android phone, so skill with jailbroken iOS as well as rooted Android is essential.  \n\nYour goal is to retrieve every photo in its original resolution\u2014no compression, no watermarks\u2014and hand them over to me, or provide a small script/tool chain I can rerun whenever new pictures are added.  \n\nDeliverables  \n\u2022 Full-size image files recovered from the app, or  \n\u2022 A clear, repeatable method (commands, script, or step-by-step guide) that lets me extract the images myself on either platform.  \n\nAcceptance Criteria  \n\u2022 Pixel dimensions of the recovered files match those reported inside the app.  \n\u2022 Files open locally with no quality loss or visible watermark.  \n\nIf you normally work with tools such as Filza, Frida, Objection, adb, or similar, just mention which ones so I can prep the devices ahead of time.",
